   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "audio",
     "lang": "en-GB",
     "text": "I am a pupil. I have a book."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Le verbe être : to be",
     "md": "En anglais, **to be** veut dire « être ».\n\n- **I am** : je suis (I am eight.)\n- **you are** : tu es (You are my friend.)\n- **he is**, **she is** : il est, elle est (She is a girl.)\n- **we are**, **they are** : nous sommes, ils sont."
    },
    {
     "type": "audio",
     "lang": "en-GB",
     "text": "I am eight. You are my friend. She is a girl. We are pupils."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Le verbe avoir : to have",
     "md": "**To have** veut dire « avoir ».\n\n- **I have** : j'ai (I have a pen.)\n- **you have** : tu as\n- **he has**, **she has** : il a, elle a (She has a bag.)\n- **we have**, **they have** : nous avons, ils ont."
    },
